  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile avgpool is the strongest direction, with scvi_n200 improving over PCA by about 6 points in accuracy and 5.5 points in F1, while image-only performance is weak. The main remaining uncertainty is whether scvi_n200 is the best RNA representation or whether scgpt can match or exceed it. config_008 keeps profile setting and aggregation fixed at the current best settings and changes only the RNA encoder, cleanly isolating the representation effect. This is the best next experiment because it can either improve the current best RNA baseline or confirm that scvi_n200 is the preferred encoder before investing in more complex multimodal or fusion settings."
